#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/dbn_classification.md:1
msgid "DBN Classification: Stacked RBM Pretraining and Supervised Fine-tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/tutorials/dbn_classification.md:3
msgid ""
"This tutorial builds on the [RBM Classification "
"tutorial](rbm_classification.md) and [Section 4.2: Restricted Boltzmann "
"Machine](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-bm-"
"restricted.md). A Deep Belief Network (DBN) stacks multiple RBM layers: "
"each RBM is pretrained greedily and unsupervised, then the whole network "
"is fine-tuned with labeled data. The key new concept is layer-wise "
"pretraining — the same RBM objective applied sequentially. This tutorial "
"also covers three training modes: unsupervised feature extraction, "
"downstream classifier, and end-to-end fine-tuning."
msgstr ""

